/*!
\page page_stFmsPointPair StFmsPointPair

\brief Pair (or group) of FMS photon points for di-photon invariant-mass analysis.

\section fmsPointPair_overview Overview

StFmsPointPair accumulates two or more StFmsPoint photon candidates and
provides the combined four-momentum, invariant mass, energy asymmetry (\c zgg),
opening distance (\c dgg), and isolation cone energies.  Its primary use is
π⁰ → γγ reconstruction in the FMS forward region (2.5 < η < 4.0).

An FPS PID word encodes each constituent photon's pre-shower classification
as a decimal digit: 1 = photon, 2 = hadron, 3 = electron.  For a 2-photon
pair, fpsPid()=11 means both are photon candidates.

\section fmsPointPair_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StFmsPointPair
\endcode

Stored in \ref page_stFmsCollection "StFmsCollection".

\section fmsPointPair_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| vector<StFmsPoint*> | mPoints | Constituent photon points (non-owning, transient). |
| StLorentzVectorD | mFourMomentum | Combined four-momentum (transient). |
| UInt_t | mFpsPid | Packed FPS PID digits, one per photon (transient). |
| Float_t[3] | mConeRadius | Isolation cone radii (transient). |
| Float_t[3] | mConeEnergy | FMS energy within each isolation cone (transient). |

\section fmsPointPair_methods Key Methods

- \c nPoints() — number of constituent photons.
- \c addPoint(StFmsPoint*) — add a photon (updates 4-momentum and FPS PID).
- \c point(int) — access photon at index i.
- \c fourMomentum(), \c energy(), \c pT(), \c eta(), \c phi() — combined kinematics.
- \c mass() — di-photon invariant mass M(γγ) [GeV/c²].
- \c zgg() — energy asymmetry |E1−E2|/(E1+E2).
- \c dgg() — photon–photon opening distance [cm].
- \c x(), \c y() — energy-weighted centroid.
- \c fpsPid() — packed FPS PID word.
- \c coneRadius(), \c coneEnergy(), \c coneEnergyFraction() — isolation.
- \c setConeEnergy() — set isolation cone energy.
- \c print() — print summary.

\section fmsPointPair_seealso See Also

\ref page_stFmsPoint "StFmsPoint",
\ref page_stFmsCluster "StFmsCluster",
\ref page_stFpsSlat "StFpsSlat"
*/
